{
  "_comment": "What each sensor can know. THE single home for these numbers (docs/adr/0042, 0059). `radar`: DCS unit type -> airborne radar; angleFromNose is the total scan arc in degrees centred on the nose (360 = a full rotating dish), rangeNm the detection range against a fighter-size target, sweepMs one full rotation or scan cycle, and an optional `caps` ({height, ssr, mode4}; mode4 = carries a Mode 4/5 interrogator, docs/adr/0066) overrides the defaults for its kind (radars.js DEFAULT_CAPS). `carrierRadar`: ship type -> surface/air search radar. `datalink`: which types are network participants (PPLI) and how often they report. `transponder`: `syntheticFor` says which coalitions' AI aircraft squawk a synthetic Mode 3/C code; `mode4For` says which coalitions' AI aircraft and ships answer a Mode 4/5 interrogation (only `own` can ever be honoured: a valid reply needs our crypto keys). Every figure is [SOURCE-DEFINED] — DCS publishes none of it, and none of it should be presented as a real system's performance.",
